  "definition": {
   "definition": "Net foreign exchange assets of the banking sector is a source of money stock (M3) in RBI's monetary survey: the total of the RBI's net foreign exchange assets and those of other banks, the latter being authorised dealers' net foreign currency balances after credit and debit foreign-currency balances. RBI's own net foreign exchange assets are its holdings of foreign currency assets and gold adjusted for foreign liabilities (net of non-monetary foreign exchange liabilities such as IMF Account No. 1). RBI compiles and publishes it fortnightly in the WSS 'Money Stock: Components and Sources' and the corresponding monetary survey, in rupees crore.",
